        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "LOL, they had 12 registered OAI participants for this AMA, and none of the top upvoted questions were answered.\n\nThe router is never going to be disabled, not on legacy models, not on GPT-5 series models - and it's unlikely December will change anything as the head of safety systems directly stated work hasn't even really started yet.\n\nIf you thought it was just \"give your ID\" as an Adult and you're good to go - you're wrong.\n\nThey want more than an adult checkbox, they want to feed the model granular details about you. Not just if you're an adult, but specifically; what else about you adds up to whatever metrics make up a checkbox for risk appetite.\n\nThe head of safety systems was the only one to address the massive negative sentiment, and out of 1.1k questions asked with 12 participants (1 of which didn't even show up), only 47 were answered - and of those 47 answers, 6 were related to the router/guardrails/adult-mode. \n\nOf those 1.1k questions, almost the entirety were related to those 3 things (router/guardrails/adult-mode).\n\nHere are some screencaps for the disappointment to come in December."
        },
